BaseSettler_recover
├── when signature is empty bytes
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSignature
├── when signature is a raw ECDSA 65-byte
│   ├── when recovered signer equals order.user
│   │   └── it should return true
│   ├── when recovered signer differs from order.user
│   │   └── it should revert with InvalidSignature
│   ├── when signature is 64 bytes EIP-2098 compact and recovers to order.user
│   │   └── it should return true
│   ├── when s is in the upper half of the curve order
│   │   └── it should revert with InvalidSignature
│   └── when signature length is neither 64 nor 65
│       └── it should revert with InvalidSignature
├── when order.user has code and is a smart wallet
│   ├── when isValidSignature returns the ERC-1271 MAGIC 0x1626ba7e
│   │   └── it should return true
│   ├── when isValidSignature returns any other value
│   │   └── it should revert with InvalidSignature
│   ├── when isValidSignature reverts
│   │   └── it should revert with InvalidSignature
│   └── when the wallet selfdestructs mid-verification
│       └── it should revert with InvalidSignature
└── when verifying a signature produced for a different settler's domain
    └── it should revert with InvalidSignature
